    description: "Sibling/follow-up to the dampener-audit item. Once the 8x4 dampener-by-surface matrix is populated, evaluate whether a shared compute_dampened_centrality(symbols, edges, surface_profile) helper is the right abstraction. The audit's findings determine the helper's interface - specifically, which dampeners are core vs. surface-conditional, and whether edge-type weighting belongs as a helper parameter or stays in compute_centrality. Do not start until the audit deliverable exists.\n\nReferences:\n- ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_04272026_1620.md (architectural finding + audit/extraction relationship)\n- ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_04272026_1545.md Q5 (\"timeline / build-vs-refactor\") - where compute_dampened_centrality was first proposed\n- Half-finished prior unification: commit 7923615524 (file-level scoring only; symbol-selection layer is what this audit/extraction pair addresses)"  # 34ad
